  {
    "ods": 17,
    "page": 2,
    "section": "G20_2024_1_Abstract",
    "arguments": [
      "All countries, and especially the G20 given their combined economic weight, must better understand, monitor and manage their spillovers to allow all countries to meet the SDGs.",
      "Curbing negative international spillovers requires multilateral solutions, especially across resource-rich and high income consumer countries.",
      "Establish inclusive processes that bring together stakeholders to co-develop multilateral policies and partnerships;",
      "The G20’s immediate aim should be to build momentum for a successful Summit of the Future by restoring trust through high-level policy discussions on international spillovers, which have the potential to accelerate the SDG progress."
    ],
    "source_file": "G20_2024__ArgsSGD17_deepseek-r1-70b.json"
  },
  {
    "ods": 17,
    "page": 3,
    "section": "G20_2024_2_Diagnosis_of_the_Issue_Addressing_Negative_Spillover_Effects_for_SDG_Achievement",
    "arguments": [
      "The G20 is therefore the right forum for overcoming structural obstacles towards the SDGs such as negative spillover effects."
    ],
